# Quality Gates

Before considering any coding task complete, verify formatting and tests.

## Formatting

- Run `npm run format` after editing source or test files so Prettier applies project style.
- If you only need to verify without writing, use `npm run format:check` — it must exit 0.
- Do not leave unformatted changes; fix formatting issues before finishing.

## Tests

- Run `npm test` after changes that affect behavior, tests, config, or dependencies.
- All Playwright tests must pass (exit code 0).
- If tests fail, fix the root cause and re-run until green — do not mark the task done with failing tests.
- When adding or changing tests, follow `.cursor/rules/playwright-typescript.mdc`.

## When to run

| Change type | Format | Tests |
|-------------|--------|-------|
| Specs, pages, services, `playwright.config.ts` | Yes | Yes |
| ESLint/Prettier config only | Optional | No |
| Docs or comments only | No | No |

Run commands from the repository root.
